From: Emon Sarkar <esarkar@uwaterloo.ca>
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: vdso: cpu_relax() without the Zihintpause static key

arch/riscv/include/asm/vdso/processor.h is also compiled into the vDSO. There,
riscv_isa_ext_keys is an undefined symbol whose GOT entry is never filled in,
so with CONFIG_JUMP_LABEL unset the static_branch_likely() check reads the key
through a NULL pointer. __vdso_clock_gettime() calls cpu_relax() only on its
seqlock retry path, that is, when another hart is updating the vDSO time data
at that moment, so user processes now and then segfault at address 0x4.
dropbear catches SIGSEGV itself and exits without a log line, so SSH/scp
sessions to the board just drop ("Connection reset by peer"): 4 of 30 16 MiB
uploads on alsaqr_xilinx_ethernet.bit. With this patch: 20 of 20 on that
bitstream and 20 of 20 on the OpenDRAM one.

Always use the div stall. CVA6 on AlSaqr has no Zihintpause, so this is the
branch that ran before. The kernel's own cpu_relax() loses the pause path too,
which it never took here. AlSaqr-only patch, not meant for upstream as is.

--- a/arch/riscv/include/asm/vdso/processor.h
+++ b/arch/riscv/include/asm/vdso/processor.h
@@ -8,26 +8,19 @@
 #include <asm/barrier.h>
 #include <asm/hwcap.h>
 
+/*
+ * AlSaqr local fix: no static_branch here. This header is also compiled into the vDSO, where
+ * riscv_isa_ext_keys is not available: its GOT entry stays 0, so the Zihintpause check read
+ * address 0x4 and __vdso_clock_gettime() segfaulted whenever it had to retry (seqlock odd while
+ * another hart updated the vDSO data). CVA6 here has no Zihintpause, so the stall is what ran.
+ */
 static inline void cpu_relax(void)
 {
-	if (!static_branch_likely(&riscv_isa_ext_keys[RISCV_ISA_EXT_KEY_ZIHINTPAUSE])) {
 #ifdef __riscv_muldiv
-		int dummy;
-		/* In lieu of a halt instruction, induce a long-latency stall. */
-		__asm__ __volatile__ ("div %0, %0, zero" : "=r" (dummy));
+	int dummy;
+	/* In lieu of a halt instruction, induce a long-latency stall. */
+	__asm__ __volatile__ ("div %0, %0, zero" : "=r" (dummy));
 #endif
-	} else {
-		/*
-		 * Reduce instruction retirement.
-		 * This assumes the PC changes.
-		 */
-#ifdef CONFIG_TOOLCHAIN_HAS_ZIHINTPAUSE
-		__asm__ __volatile__ ("pause");
-#else
-		/* Encoding of the pause instruction */
-		__asm__ __volatile__ (".4byte 0x100000F");
-#endif
-	}
 	barrier();
 }
 
